I've written the Day 230 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit step made no commit because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the file is on disk only, and that's where the planner reads it. I restored Cargo.lock after probing, so the tree is clean at 6b64946a.

Main finding: the move to yoagent 0.25.5 is blocked by one test, and that test is the intended safeguard. The creator's new start-of-session dependency update (Step 1a, 6b64946a) tried yoagent 0.25.2 → 0.25.5 this session and was rolled back. I repeated it by hand:
• Build: passes.
• Unit tests (`cargo test --bin yoyo`): 6244 passed, 0 failed.
• Integration tests: one failure, doc_version_claims::every_dependency_version_claim_names_the_pinned_yoagent_version. It fails because 15 notes in the code and docs still say they were checked against 0.25.2: CLAUDE.md, 4 spots in ARCHITECTURE.md, and 10 across cost.rs, gasp.rs, prompt.rs, tool_wrappers*.rs and tools.rs. Each needs its paragraph re-read against 0.25.5 before the version is bumped.
• Cost of leaving it: every session pays an extra build plus a full test run that is certain to fail, then rebuilds on the old lock.
• What landing it gets: the upstream fix for the search problem I reported (the rg config fix, #1023 item 1), a search that ends abnormally no longer reporting "No matches", and the yoagent skill that the creator's other new commit (21a75910) can now load.

Other findings:
• #1033 (filed by the creator): the Day-230 commit body said "Seen, not fixed: #1032.", which GitHub read as a closing keyword and used to close #1032; he reopened it. The fix is to add the rule to skills/evolve/SKILL.md. It's small and should apply to every commit message this session, including the upgrade.
• New and not yet filed: a malformed .yoyo.toml loads without any warning. With an unterminated quote, the model id keeps a stray leading ", and the API returns a 404 with no hint that the file is broken. The cause is the hand-written line parser in src/config.rs:1984, which has no way to report errors. Claude Code just fixed the same gap in its -p mode.
• Small, already-specified product fixes: #1032 (/cd back to the starting folder wrongly warns that its own settings aren't applied) and #1030 (a typo'd cost budget silently turns the budget off).
• Two files are within 14 lines of the size limit that fails cargo test: commands_risk_unhittable.rs and format/mod.rs. Any task touching them has to split them or update the size register.
• Research: I read Claude Code's changelog for 2.1.296–2.1.300 and saved the relevant items to yopedia. One item I checked and cleared: their "hook fails to start → action goes through anyway" bug doesn't apply here, because yoyo already blocks the action when a pre-hook fails to start or times out.

Suggested order for the planner: the 0.25.5 upgrade first, then #1033, then one of #1032, #1030 or the config-file warning.

